From: Greg Burd <greg@burd.me>
Subject: [PATCH 0/2] OpenZFS 2.3.6 Integration for OSv Unikernel
Date: Thu, 20 Mar 2026 11:30:00 -0400

This patch series adds complete OpenZFS 2.3.6 support to OSv, a unikernel
designed for cloud applications. The integration follows OpenZFS's
platform-split architecture and adds a new OSv platform alongside existing
Linux and FreeBSD implementations.

## Motivation

OSv is a cloud-focused unikernel that runs a single application per VM with
minimal overhead. Adding ZFS support enables:

- Compression (lz4) for reduced storage costs in cloud environments
- Snapshots for fast application state management
- Data integrity through checksums
- Efficient storage for containerized workloads

## Architecture

These patches implement the OSv platform layer using OpenZFS 2.3.6's clean
platform-split design:

```
openzfs/
├── include/os/
│   ├── linux/      # Linux platform
│   ├── freebsd/    # FreeBSD platform
│   └── osv/        # OSv platform (new)
└── module/os/
    ├── linux/      # Linux implementation
    ├── freebsd/    # FreeBSD implementation
    └── osv/        # OSv implementation (new)
```

This approach keeps all OSv-specific code isolated in the platform directories
without polluting common code with `#ifdef __OSV__` guards.

## Design Decisions

### 1. Simplified Memory Management
OSv lacks slab allocators (uma_zone/kmem_cache), so we use simple kmem_alloc()
for all allocations. This matches the pattern used by smaller platforms.

### 2. Manual Reference Counting
OSv's vnode implementation doesn't provide automatic reference counting, so
znodes include an explicit z_ref_cnt field with manual zfs_zhold/zfs_zrele
tracking.

### 3. ABD-Based I/O
Block I/O uses ABD (Aggregate Buffer Descriptors) with abd_borrow_buf() for
integration with OSv's bio layer, following the FreeBSD vdev_geom fallback
pattern.

### 4. Automatic Pool Upgrade
Pools created with legacy ZFS versions (< 5000) are automatically upgraded to
the feature flags era on first import. This ensures compatibility with older
ZFS images while enabling modern features.

## Implementation Summary

**Patch 1/2: Platform Layer and SPL**
- 46 SPL (Solaris Porting Layer) headers in include/os/osv/spl/
- 7 platform headers in include/os/osv/zfs/sys/
- 15 core implementation files in module/os/osv/zfs/
- Block device integration via OSv bio layer
- ARC memory management adapted for OSv
- ~15,400 lines

**Patch 2/2: File Operations and Auto-Upgrade**
- File/directory operations (zfs_vnops_os.c, zfs_znode_os.c, zfs_dir.c)
- Platform-specific implementations (abd_os.c, spl_uio.c)
- Automatic pool upgrade feature (zfs_auto_upgrade.c)
- VFS integration with upgrade hooks
- ~1,300 lines

**Total: ~16,700 lines** of OSv-specific integration code

## Testing

The integration has been tested with:
- Pool creation and mounting
- File operations (read, write, getattr, setattr)
- Directory operations (lookup, create, remove)
- Compression (lz4)
- Snapshots
- Legacy pool upgrade (version 28 -> 5000)

## Maintenance

These patches will be maintained in the OSv repository and updated as new
OpenZFS versions are released. The clean platform split makes updates
straightforward.

